{"corrected_text": "I think the family matters a lot to everybody. We don't choose our parents and children, but we can choose a good husband or a wife. My parents divorced when I was 16 years old, so I don't have a close relationship with my mom and dad, although I'm very grateful to my mom for great support in the most difficult times of my life. My mother has a lot of friends and she is quite happy. My dad has a new family and it seems he is fine too. 

My son is 13 years old and we understand each other very well. I'm a friend to him rather than a strict mother. He does not conceal anything from me, as I try to understand what he really needs and support him.

My husband is also my best friend, as I don't have anybody closer than him. We speak about everything and respect each other. Sometimes we quarrel, but it doesn't last long. I'm happy, as I had always dreamt of such a family."}

{"corrected_text": "I think it is fair to say basketball is one of the most popular sports on the planet, both in the number of viewers and the number of players. There is probably an array of reasons to explain such a phenomenon, but for me, that happens for one particular reason; the shot clock. The shot clock is a timer that dictates the amount of time during which one team can keep possession of the ball. The idea behind it is to quicken the pace of the game and prevent it from becoming stalled. A curious fact is that, out of the five most popular sports in the world, only basketball keeps track of possession time and to me that's exactly what sets it apart from the others.

While watching or playing any kind of sport, there's nothing worse than a team or a player trying to waste time until the clock runs out, the game becomes dull and boring and you can't enjoy the excitement that only the up-tempo style of play can provide. The bottom line is; a fast-paced game is a much more exciting experience for players and viewers than a slow paced one and that makes the "shot clock" fundamental to the dynamics of the game.

And for anyone trying to become a good basketball player, the two most important things to understand (as it is for most sports in general) are the values of practice and awareness. Practice is the one thing that can increase the probability of desirable results and awareness is what gives you the ability to adapt to different situations, and the combination of the two is the only way to success. So if you want to be a good player, you need to put your energy and focus on practice and stay alert and survey the court at all times so you can be aware of what is happening around you."}

{"corrected_text": "I think today's television is still  good value, because there is more choice than ever before. You can watch whatever you want, whenever you want! There's always something to watch for everybody.

Of course, I think that we shouldn't watch too much television. I think that's the only negative point about today's television, because maybe there's too much choice! Some people just watch TV the whole day long, and stay in their houses. They just can't stop watching television, because there's just so much that they like to watch.

I think that we should promise ourselves that we will just watch a maximum of 1 hour's TV every day. In that way, we can enjoy all the new technology of today, and all the enjoyable TV programmes!"}

{"corrected_text": "It had been a long and rainy day. Tom had been working all day and was very tired and hungry. He decided to go and have dinner at a restaurant which was very near his office. He put his raincoat on, took his umbrella and headed to the street.  He walked briskly to the restaurant, and tried to be as happy as he could.

The restaurant was almost full. As usual, he decided to sit at the bar and order some fish and chips. The waiter, Anthony, knew him and they talked to each other about how their day had been, while he served him the usual beer. Tom had a first drink and looked around the place. He suddenly recognized someone, Molly. Surprised, he thought he hadn't seen her for a long time.

Tom and Molly were classmates at secondary school. She seemed to be having a drink with a friend at the bar. She was calling the waiter, and unexpectedly saw Tom sitting at a table alone. They both smiled at each other, and Tom went over to her to say hello. It was an exciting encounter, and they were both very happy to see each other again. As they talked they came to realize that they had been working in offices which were very near for almost a year. They felt really happy together, and Molly asked Tom for a date. It had been a very long and tiring day, but Tom felt he had achieved something really good."}

{"corrected_text": "Peter looked at his watch and knew he had to do something immediately. He had been stuck in this blizzard for a long time. He didn't know what to do. He tried to call someone, but the line didn't work. He was starting to get agitated, he was arriving late to his sister's wedding. It was probably the best day of her life and he wasn't there with her.

When the first hour had passed, he decided he would walk. When he opened the door, a cold wind whipped him hard but he didn't care about it and kept going. The sky was cloudy, the temperature was below zero, the wind made him not able to walk and it was then that he realized why is sister was celebrating her wedding on this date.

He began to feel wet and that was when he noticed that it was raining heavily. He couldn't believe it, but he couldn't stop walking. He had to get to the church. Peter opened the door and everybody turned around to look at him. He was wet, cold, starving, and outside the weather had worsened, the road was flooded and the cars couldn't pass. But Peter did not regret having walked in the pouring rain, because he had been with his sister on her special day."}

{"corrected_text": "Travelling by car is much more convenient, as many people say, but public transport is much better for the environment. There are now 8 billion people living on our earth and if everyone drove a car, the pollution would be so great, that we couldn't live here anymore. 

