{"corrected_text": "The game of gentlemen is my favourite game. Yes, I mean cricket. In my country, we follow cricket like a religion. Cricket is played by 11 players, which includes a captain, a wicket keeper and the rest are batsmen and bowlers. A player who can bat and bowl is called an all-rounder. This game is played in three format i.e. Test Cricket (5 day game), One day Cricket, and Twenty-Twenty.

Test cricket is an old format and I love this format as it really tests the players' skills and only the best player can achieve success in this format. But as this takes 5 days, many people don't have time to watch this game and its losing its popularity with the younger generation.

One day cricket is played often."}

{"corrected_text": "When I was in Bali, I had a great night that I will always remember. My husband and I went to a dinner on the beach of our hotel.

The weather was very good and we enjoyed having dinner barefoot, sitting on the sand. The dinner was delicious and we tasted lots of new flavours of Balinese food. After dinner, we saw an interesting show of Balinese dance and music.

When we thought that the night had ended, we had the perfect dessert. Despite it being very dark, we could see something moving on the sand. It was very big... We couldn't believe what we were seeing. It was a very big and beautiful turtle! But... it was lost and couldn't find the way to the water. We shouted and two waiters of the hotel came quickly. They turned the turtle and took it to the water, where they freed it. Then the turtle started swimming and disappeared from our sight. We were very happy because of seeing the turtle and hope to go back to Bali to see it again."}

