{"corrected_text": "Clearly, travelling in your own car is much more comfortable than on public transport. For this reason, many people now believe that there is no future for public transport. These people believe that over the next few years we will see a severe decline in the number of people using buses, trains, trams, etc. to get to places. In my opinion, this is disappointing for a number of reasons.

First of all, public transport brings us closer to other people. We share moments with those people using the same mode of transport as us. Also, it is an excellent way of saving the environment. By using public transport, we reduce our carbon footprint and help to save the Earth. Furthermore, we also save time: as cities become bigger it becomes more and more difficult to park, which in turn leads to us wasting time looking for somewhere to park, or wasting money on expensive car parks.

In conclusion, I believe that public transport should be a necessary part of everybody's life. We should use it every day to save the Earth, money, and time."}

